(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The module _thread (PY6f; Modules/_threadmodule.c): threads over goroutines under the GIL (thread_gil.go,"] [10 1 "// PYS10 (a)), locks and re-entrant locks whose waits release the GIL (on the main thread interruptible by a"] [11 1 "// signal's handler), thread handles (start_joinable_thread, join, _shutdown joining the non-daemon threads at"] [12 1 "// the end), thread identity, and _local, thread-local data: one dict per thread, swapped in at each access."] [21 1 "// pyLock is a lock: a token in ch when it is free (acquire receives it, release sends it back)."] [34 1 "// acquire takes the lock: at once when it is free; else, blocking, within timeout (negative: no limit)."] [56 1 "// pyRLock is a re-entrant lock: its owner's ident (0: none), the count, the lock under it."] [65 1 "// threadHandle is a thread's handle (ThreadHandle): its ident, its state, done closed when it ends."] [68 14 "// handleNotStarted, handleRunning, handleDone"] [71 15 "// by start_joinable_thread (joinable)"] [93 1 "// timeoutMax is TIMEOUT_MAX in seconds (PY_TIMEOUT_MAX / 1e6 on Linux)."] [96 1 "// lockAcquireArgs reads acquire(blocking=True, timeout=-1): blocking and the timeout (negative: none)."] [133 1 "// timeoutArg is a join's or a get's timeout: None or absent no limit (negative), else seconds."] [154 1 "// currentIdent is the running thread's ident."] [157 1 "// allThreads are the started threads that run, oldest first, with their idents (queue 220: faulthandler's dumps read"] [158 1 "// them from goroutines that do not hold the GIL, so under a lock of their own and not from threadInfos)."] [165 1 "// threadsNewestFirst are the threads as CPython's interpreter lists them: the newest first, the main thread last."] [179 1 "// threadIdentOf is t's ident as the registry holds it (the main thread's mainThreadIdent)."] [189 1 "// mainInterpThread is the main thread of the running interpreter (set by NewInterp)."] [214 1 "// shutdownHandles are the non-daemon threads' handles, joined by _shutdown."] [217 1 "// startThread runs fn(args) in a new thread under the GIL (thread_run): SystemExit ends it silently, another"] [218 1 "// exception goes to sys.unraisablehook."] [253 1 "// threadOSNames are the OS threads' names (pthread_setname_np's), by ident: one OS thread's in every interpreter (queue 230)."] [256 1 "// threadsAllowed is do_start_new_thread's checks of the interpreter's config (queue 230)."] [268 1 "// writeUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable: sys.unraisablehook called with the exception, the message and the"] [269 1 "// object, or, when it is the default hook, CPython's text on stderr."] [275 2 "// format_unraisable_v: an exception with no traceback gets the current frame's (PyTraceBack_Here)"] [281 3 "// write_unraisable_exc: no sys.stderr (None, or sys's dictionary cleared at shutdown) writes nothing"] [314 1 "// WaitForThreadShutdown is Py_FinalizeEx's wait_for_thread_shutdown: threading._shutdown() when threading was"] [315 1 "// imported, its error printed."] [334 1 "// localState is a _local's per-thread dicts and its constructor's arguments (localobject)."] [343 1 "// localDict makes o's dict the running thread's, made (and __init__ called again, as CPython's"] [344 1 "// _ldict) on the thread's first access."] [802 4 "// PyErr_SetInterruptEx: only a Python handler is tripped; on the main thread it runs at once (CPython's"] [803 4 "// next eval breaker check is at the call's return)"] [810 3 "// set_name and _get_name: the thread's name as pthread_setname_np keeps it on Linux, encoded in utf-8,"] [811 3 "// cut at a NUL and at _NAME_MAXLEN (15) bytes, read back by os.fsdecode's rule"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[104 34] [170 35] [170 43] [173 26] [183 35] [234 34] [235 29] [276 25] [280 32] [282 37] [299 101] [300 37] [301 48] [328 32] [355 21] [367 56] [368 70] [504 40] [523 50] [693 38] [724 34] [777 34] [781 36] [804 26] [836 43]]} (go/file "builtins_thread.go